WEBVTT

00:20.854 --> 00:25.692
‎30 MILES NORTH OF THE MIDPOINT
‎RED CANYON

00:36.911 --> 00:37.996
‎There it is.

00:42.625 --> 00:45.252
‎That's the Zombie Horse?

00:45.253 --> 00:48.965
‎It's just a lousy mural
‎of a vicious-looking horse.

01:02.979 --> 01:04.606
‎What are you doing with that?

01:06.232 --> 01:08.818
‎Johnny, do you have any wire?

01:12.363 --> 01:14.574
‎Hey! What the hell are you doing?

01:15.283 --> 01:17.493
‎The Zombie Horse heals injuries.

01:17.494 --> 01:19.578
‎This must be for stitching.

01:19.579 --> 01:20.955
‎My father was a doctor.

01:21.539 --> 01:22.707
‎A doctor?

01:23.958 --> 01:26.752
‎This thread can heal injuries,
‎up to a point.

01:26.753 --> 01:30.380
‎It'll even reattach flesh
‎that's been blown off.

01:30.381 --> 01:34.803
‎How does that even work?
‎There's no way!

01:35.678 --> 01:38.514
‎But if it really can heal...

01:38.515 --> 01:41.601
‎Like the Steel Ball, it's something more.

01:42.977 --> 01:45.104
‎Like a Stand ability.

01:48.024 --> 01:49.025
‎No.

01:49.609 --> 01:53.363
‎Just like the letter said,
‎it's a gift from the king.

01:54.072 --> 01:57.617
‎My father never writes letters.

01:58.868 --> 02:01.246
‎An executioner and a doctor.

02:01.746 --> 02:03.915
‎Even if I asked him about it,

02:04.499 --> 02:06.334
‎he'd never tell me.

02:08.253 --> 02:11.589
‎1875 KINGDOM OF NAPLES

02:19.347 --> 02:20.807
‎Good morning, sir.

02:22.892 --> 02:26.187
‎Gyro Zeppeli. How old are you now?

02:26.771 --> 02:27.981
‎I'm nine, sir.

02:42.537 --> 02:44.789
‎STEEL BALL RUN
‎JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

03:59.572 --> 04:03.409
‎#06
‎GYRO ZEPPELI’S DESTINY

04:04.160 --> 04:06.411
‎I'm off to the castle.

04:06.412 --> 04:07.913
‎Take care, dear.

04:07.914 --> 04:09.665
‎Listen, Gyro.

04:09.666 --> 04:12.251
‎Every man needs a map.

04:12.252 --> 04:15.629
‎A map in his heart to guide him
‎across the wilderness.

04:15.630 --> 04:18.883
‎-Never forget that.
‎-Yes, Father.

04:19.467 --> 04:22.928
‎Gregorio Zeppeli, Gyro Zeppeli's father.

04:22.929 --> 04:25.682
‎He was a doctor.

04:26.391 --> 04:30.352
‎He treated the rich and the poor alike

04:30.353 --> 04:32.730
‎at his family clinic.

04:37.068 --> 04:41.698
‎Gyro, how would you get the Steel Ball
‎out of my fist?

04:47.078 --> 04:50.497
‎Ow! Not like that, Gyro!

04:50.498 --> 04:53.041
‎I'm talking about the Spin!

04:53.042 --> 04:57.422
‎I'm asking how you'd get it out
‎using the Spin.

04:58.881 --> 05:01.175
‎That's impossible, Father.

05:01.718 --> 05:03.302
‎Listen, Gyro.

05:03.303 --> 05:06.013
‎You spend all your time riding horses,

05:06.014 --> 05:11.269
‎but you must master the Spin
‎by the time you're 13.

05:14.230 --> 05:17.859
‎The Spin is the source of all power.

05:18.401 --> 05:20.986
‎My father taught me.

05:20.987 --> 05:24.364
‎His father taught him too.

05:24.365 --> 05:25.741
‎Why?

05:25.742 --> 05:29.746
‎What's the connection
‎between the Steel Ball and our family?

05:30.330 --> 05:33.790
‎Because every man in the Zeppeli family
‎has done so.

05:33.791 --> 05:35.710
‎I know you can do it.

05:37.337 --> 05:38.670
‎You may go now.

05:38.671 --> 05:39.672
‎Yes, Father.

05:42.800 --> 05:45.052
‎Putting it in a fist

05:45.053 --> 05:47.847
‎is easier than taking it out.

05:50.183 --> 05:52.143
‎No way! When did he...

05:55.354 --> 05:58.232
‎FOUR YEARS LATER

06:01.152 --> 06:03.279
‎Gyro. How old are you now?

06:05.823 --> 06:07.325
‎I'm 13, sir.

06:08.785 --> 06:11.036
‎I'm off to the castle.

06:11.037 --> 06:12.455
‎Take care, dear.

06:13.122 --> 06:14.706
‎-Gyro.
‎-Yes, Father?

06:14.707 --> 06:17.627
‎You're coming with me today.

06:18.669 --> 06:19.670
‎What?

06:29.180 --> 06:31.890
‎Aren't we going to the castle?

06:31.891 --> 06:34.143
‎We already passed it.

06:37.438 --> 06:38.439
‎Gyro.

06:39.524 --> 06:42.359
‎Every man needs a map.

06:42.360 --> 06:45.655
‎A map in his heart to guide him
‎across the wilderness.

06:47.281 --> 06:50.827
‎Listen well. You're the eldest son
‎of the Zeppeli family.

06:51.452 --> 06:53.995
‎You must protect your family.

06:53.996 --> 06:57.916
‎A person's happiness
‎lies within their family.

06:57.917 --> 07:01.878
‎Protecting your family
‎means protecting your country.

07:01.879 --> 07:04.923
‎If a family falls apart,

07:04.924 --> 07:09.636
‎you dishonor both your ancestors
‎and your descendants.

07:09.637 --> 07:11.513
‎Never forget that.

07:11.514 --> 07:12.557
‎Yes, Father.

07:21.149 --> 07:22.358
‎This place is...

07:24.610 --> 07:28.196
‎Starting today,
‎you'll assist me with my work.

07:28.197 --> 07:30.907
‎Your work as a doctor?

07:30.908 --> 07:34.077
‎This duty was entrusted to us

07:34.078 --> 07:37.248
‎380 years ago by the king.

07:37.748 --> 07:41.585
‎It has been the Zeppeli family's duty
‎ever since.

07:41.586 --> 07:44.338
‎It has endured through every king's reign.

07:45.006 --> 07:47.632
‎Approach it with the utmost solemnity.

07:47.633 --> 07:51.219
‎Judicial Official!
‎Please come to the courtyard!

07:51.220 --> 07:52.554
‎No!

07:52.555 --> 07:55.849
‎-He's out of control. Thrashing about!
‎-Damn you all!

07:55.850 --> 07:59.895
‎Where's the priest?
‎Couldn't he prepare him for this?

07:59.896 --> 08:01.230
‎We can't handle the convict.

08:02.148 --> 08:04.984
‎He has no peace of mind.

08:06.110 --> 08:07.111
‎Gyro.

08:07.612 --> 08:10.948
‎Wait here. I'll tell you what to do.

08:22.376 --> 08:23.544
‎Father!

08:26.547 --> 08:28.048
‎Stop!

08:28.049 --> 08:31.092
‎No! I don't wanna die!

08:31.093 --> 08:32.469
‎I don't wanna die!

08:32.470 --> 08:35.932
‎-Don't move. Quiet your mind.
‎-Damn you!

08:36.933 --> 08:39.684
‎I don't wanna die! Stop!

08:39.685 --> 08:40.728
‎Quiet your mind...

09:20.059 --> 09:22.979
‎You will cleanse the sword.

09:24.272 --> 09:27.483
‎Your duty begins here.

09:33.573 --> 09:35.533
‎Yes, Father.

09:40.663 --> 09:43.623
‎Wherever capital punishment
‎is upheld by law,

09:43.624 --> 09:47.253
‎someone must carry it out.

09:47.962 --> 09:52.924
‎An executioner must know
‎the human body inside and out.

09:52.925 --> 09:57.555
‎The Zeppeli ancestors studied medicine
‎and mastered the art of combat.

09:58.306 --> 10:01.641
‎They also created the Spin

10:01.642 --> 10:04.269
‎to keep the body at peace.

10:04.270 --> 10:06.980
‎The Spin exists not for pain,

10:06.981 --> 10:09.274
‎but for peace.

10:09.275 --> 10:12.153
‎Each generation refined it further.

10:13.070 --> 10:14.738
‎Carrying out executions.

10:14.739 --> 10:19.492
‎That is the Zeppeli family's destiny
‎for the past 380 years.

10:19.493 --> 10:23.122
‎12 YEARS LATER

10:23.873 --> 10:26.041
‎Stay back, you bastard!

10:26.042 --> 10:30.420
‎If I'm dying, I'm taking
‎as many of you with me as I can!

10:30.421 --> 10:33.007
‎One step closer and I'll kill him!

10:34.133 --> 10:35.843
‎Help me!

10:41.474 --> 10:43.934
‎Are you crazy?

10:54.528 --> 10:57.781
‎It's twisting... It's tightening!

10:57.782 --> 10:59.449
‎Get him!

10:59.450 --> 11:01.493
‎You bastard!

11:01.494 --> 11:02.828
‎Well done, Gyro!

11:03.412 --> 11:05.790
‎Just like Mr. Zeppeli's son!

11:11.045 --> 11:13.673
‎Gyro. How old are you now?

11:15.591 --> 11:17.093
‎I'm 24, sir.

11:17.802 --> 11:21.262
‎When Gyro Zeppeli turned 25,

11:21.263 --> 11:25.308
‎he was to inherit his father's position.

11:25.309 --> 11:27.310
‎As his successor.

11:27.311 --> 11:30.980
‎Everything was as it should be.

11:30.981 --> 11:32.691
‎Had things stayed that way.

11:34.735 --> 11:39.615
‎That was until a boy named Marco,
‎who polished shoes at a noble estate...

11:40.366 --> 11:41.826
‎Sentenced to death.

11:43.119 --> 11:44.202
‎BOY SENTENCED TO DEATH
‎TREASON

11:44.203 --> 11:46.497
‎...was sentenced to death.

11:52.044 --> 11:53.379
‎Excuse me...

11:54.296 --> 11:55.339
‎What?

11:56.006 --> 11:58.258
‎Is there anything I can do?

11:58.259 --> 11:59.717
‎Something you can do?

11:59.718 --> 12:01.845
‎I want to work.

12:01.846 --> 12:05.515
‎When I went to serve
‎as a live-in servant for the baron,

12:05.516 --> 12:06.933
‎my father told me.

12:06.934 --> 12:09.227
‎He said if I stayed humble
‎and worked hard,

12:09.228 --> 12:11.604
‎I'd earn their respect someday.

12:11.605 --> 12:13.315
‎He said I'd find happiness.

12:14.859 --> 12:19.821
‎My grandfather did this work,
‎and so did his father.

12:19.822 --> 12:22.031
‎I can sew anything.

12:22.032 --> 12:24.410
‎No one shines shoes better than me.

12:24.994 --> 12:27.496
‎I can polish silverware until it shines.

12:28.581 --> 12:32.834
‎I can memorize every dish
‎and every wine, and--

12:32.835 --> 12:34.211
‎That's enough! Stop!

12:37.506 --> 12:41.718
‎Whatever it is, I'll do it carefully.
‎I'll do it well.

12:41.719 --> 12:43.219
‎Just like my father said--

12:43.220 --> 12:44.555
‎Don't talk to me!

12:46.140 --> 12:47.766
‎Never again. Got it?

12:52.480 --> 12:53.564
‎Never again...

12:58.444 --> 13:01.446
‎JUDICIAL OFFICIAL ZEPPELI
‎CHALLENGED THE BOY'S GUILTY VERDICT

13:01.447 --> 13:03.448
‎BUT TO NO AVAIL

13:03.449 --> 13:06.451
‎You've overstepped, Gyro.

13:06.452 --> 13:10.371
‎All you've done is throw the country
‎into turmoil.

13:10.372 --> 13:15.210
‎Our family's duty isn't to decide
‎guilt or innocence.

13:15.211 --> 13:19.130
‎Father, I only want to be convinced
‎this is just.

13:19.131 --> 13:21.591
‎Personal conviction has no place here!

13:21.592 --> 13:25.012
‎Not even for the vilest criminals.

13:25.596 --> 13:28.348
‎But that boy...

13:28.349 --> 13:32.728
‎He had nothing to do
‎with the plot of his employer, the baron.

13:33.312 --> 13:35.104
‎He only polished shoes.

13:35.105 --> 13:40.235
‎We carry out the king's orders.
‎Nothing more.

13:40.236 --> 13:43.738
‎The law is the law.
‎Stay out of the legal process.

13:43.739 --> 13:46.449
‎It is beyond personal conviction.

13:46.450 --> 13:48.577
‎All is God's will!

13:49.828 --> 13:52.248
‎He has been sentenced to death.

13:53.582 --> 13:55.917
‎Soon I'll turn 25

13:55.918 --> 13:57.753
‎and succeed you.

13:58.337 --> 14:03.092
‎Will my first duty be to behead
‎that nine-year-old boy?

14:06.804 --> 14:09.889
‎I never made friends.

14:09.890 --> 14:11.724
‎I don't keep pets.

14:11.725 --> 14:14.310
‎I dine only with my family.

14:14.311 --> 14:17.522
‎I don't even invite relatives
‎into my home.

14:17.523 --> 14:21.569
‎I never keep a diary or write letters.

14:22.152 --> 14:27.115
‎If my hand were off
‎by even a tenth of a millimeter,

14:27.116 --> 14:30.660
‎the execution would fail.

14:30.661 --> 14:35.374
‎Worse, it would inflict
‎unimaginable suffering on the condemned.

14:38.586 --> 14:42.505
‎That's caused by sentiment.

14:42.506 --> 14:43.756
‎Sentiment...

14:43.757 --> 14:47.886
‎Personal ties lead to sentiment.

14:47.887 --> 14:50.723
‎Sentiment leaves your heart vulnerable.

14:52.016 --> 14:53.142
‎My son.

14:53.726 --> 14:56.519
‎A sentimental heart is dangerous.

14:56.520 --> 14:59.148
‎It can make your future miserable.

14:59.732 --> 15:01.984
‎Never forget, my son.

15:04.820 --> 15:09.574
‎High treason
‎was the gravest of all crimes.

15:09.575 --> 15:13.078
‎Even a boy who did nothing
‎but polish shoes...

15:13.662 --> 15:18.208
‎Such was the law of that nation
‎in those days.

15:41.649 --> 15:44.568
‎TWO MONTHS EARLIER

15:51.283 --> 15:53.494
‎"All is God's will."

15:54.119 --> 15:55.329
‎Is it really?

15:58.207 --> 16:00.876
‎Gyro. How old are you now?

16:02.002 --> 16:04.004
‎You already know that.

16:06.048 --> 16:08.883
‎So why did you send for me?

16:08.884 --> 16:11.010
‎Need advice or something?

16:11.011 --> 16:13.346
‎Then ask someone else.

16:13.347 --> 16:16.350
‎Aren't you the one
‎who's got something on your mind?

16:16.976 --> 16:19.268
‎About the boy.

16:19.269 --> 16:20.729
‎The boy...

16:22.898 --> 16:25.358
‎I'm proud of my family,

16:25.359 --> 16:27.026
‎and I'll succeed my father.

16:27.027 --> 16:29.737
‎This duty is my destiny.

16:29.738 --> 16:31.448
‎That'll never change.

16:32.574 --> 16:34.993
‎It never has, and it never will.

16:34.994 --> 16:36.912
‎But I...

16:40.082 --> 16:42.126
‎I just want to be convinced!

16:42.751 --> 16:47.213
‎I want this duty from the king
‎to be a source of pride.

16:47.214 --> 16:51.175
‎I have to be convinced!
‎That's where my pride comes from!

16:51.176 --> 16:53.511
‎I'd give my life for that pride!

16:53.512 --> 16:56.055
‎High treason is a grave crime.

16:56.056 --> 16:58.142
‎But laws can be wrong.

16:58.726 --> 17:03.688
‎I can't accept an uninvolved boy
‎being condemned to death!

17:03.689 --> 17:06.400
‎I have to be convinced it's just!

17:07.192 --> 17:11.320
‎Would you risk your life for that boy?

17:11.321 --> 17:12.864
‎Is that what you're saying?

17:12.865 --> 17:14.490
‎I want to be sure.

17:14.491 --> 17:15.575
‎What?

17:15.576 --> 17:17.827
‎Let me ask you again.

17:17.828 --> 17:20.496
‎If that boy could be cleared,

17:20.497 --> 17:22.458
‎would you risk your life?

17:23.167 --> 17:25.752
‎What the hell are you talking about?

17:25.753 --> 17:27.087
‎Can you?

17:33.343 --> 17:35.679
‎Yes. I want to save him.

17:37.931 --> 17:40.392
‎He only polished shoes.

17:41.018 --> 17:44.396
‎Is it foolish for a Zeppeli man
‎to feel this way?

17:44.897 --> 17:48.442
‎There's only one way
‎to overturn the sentence.

17:49.234 --> 17:51.778
‎If a war were to break out,

17:51.779 --> 17:53.946
‎and the Kingdom emerged victorious...

17:53.947 --> 17:59.578
‎The king must grant a royal pardon
‎for a kingdom-wide celebration.

18:00.746 --> 18:04.541
‎A royal pardon is an act of clemency
‎that reduces a criminal's sentence!

18:05.167 --> 18:07.251
‎A royal pardon?

18:07.252 --> 18:09.754
‎Yes. He will definitely issue one.

18:09.755 --> 18:12.173
‎No! That's not my point.

18:12.174 --> 18:14.468
‎Where would a war even break out?

18:15.719 --> 18:17.346
‎"The Steel Ball Run"...

18:18.305 --> 18:21.850
‎You've mastered the Steel Ball technique,
‎Gyro Zeppeli!

18:22.518 --> 18:25.353
‎You can win it.
‎That's why I'm telling you this.

18:25.354 --> 18:29.774
‎The whole world sees winning this race
‎as the equivalent

18:29.775 --> 18:32.361
‎of winning a war!

18:32.861 --> 18:35.321
‎If a rider from our Kingdom wins,

18:35.322 --> 18:38.867
‎our king will grant a royal pardon!

18:41.078 --> 18:43.538
‎This is my map.

18:43.539 --> 18:47.167
‎The map in my heart to guide me
‎across the wilderness!

18:58.595 --> 19:00.596
‎Only 15 miles to the finish.

19:00.597 --> 19:03.307
‎Just because there aren't any officials...
‎That bastard!

19:03.308 --> 19:06.269
‎That terrorist
‎is seventh in the first stage...

19:06.270 --> 19:08.437
‎Fritz von Stroheim, from Germany!

19:08.438 --> 19:09.897
‎You know him too?

19:09.898 --> 19:13.443
‎No. Nobody I know has hair like that.

19:13.944 --> 19:15.821
‎He's coming again, Gyro!

19:19.324 --> 19:20.450
‎Gyro!

19:31.378 --> 19:34.256
‎It hurts!

19:37.176 --> 19:40.887
‎Damn! Who the hell are you?

19:40.888 --> 19:42.930
‎The Spin of the Steel Ball...

19:42.931 --> 19:45.224
‎They can grind away matter

19:45.225 --> 19:47.810
‎and even control human muscles.

19:47.811 --> 19:52.023
‎They can even harden your skin
‎enough to stop bullets, huh?

19:52.024 --> 19:53.400
‎You...

19:54.943 --> 19:56.277
‎Gyro!

19:56.278 --> 19:59.155
‎Drop them, Gyro Zeppeli!

19:59.156 --> 20:01.532
‎Drop the Steel Ball right now

20:01.533 --> 20:05.870
‎or your friend and your horse are next.

20:05.871 --> 20:08.497
‎Or you can throw them at me if you like.

20:08.498 --> 20:12.377
‎Then I'll prove my gun's faster.

20:13.170 --> 20:16.589
‎Drop them? My Steel Ball?

20:16.590 --> 20:18.967
‎You sure you want that?

20:20.052 --> 20:23.387
‎If you're that determined,

20:23.388 --> 20:25.766
‎then I really will.

20:32.689 --> 20:33.899
‎There. I let go.

20:51.416 --> 20:52.584
‎Terrorists...

20:53.585 --> 20:57.005
‎Just what kind of country are you from?

20:58.048 --> 21:03.302
‎Even if winning this race
‎symbolizes national glory,

21:03.303 --> 21:04.429
‎this is too much!

21:05.264 --> 21:07.848
‎Why do they keep coming after you?

21:07.849 --> 21:09.934
‎They're only after you.

21:09.935 --> 21:11.686
‎It's just a race!

21:11.687 --> 21:13.980
‎I feel like there's something deeper...

21:13.981 --> 21:18.485
‎some old feud
‎between the terrorists and your country.

21:21.446 --> 21:23.532
‎I serve the king.

21:24.116 --> 21:26.909
‎If I win, he will grant a royal pardon.

21:26.910 --> 21:28.327
‎That's all.

21:28.328 --> 21:29.787
‎A royal pardon?

21:29.788 --> 21:33.332
‎I'm crossing this continent
‎in first place.

21:33.333 --> 21:36.002
‎If you think this is too dangerous,

21:36.003 --> 21:38.463
‎you'd better go your own way.

21:44.970 --> 21:47.264
‎I must have been hurt when I fell off.

21:48.140 --> 21:50.058
‎But I don't feel any pain.

23:30.951 --> 23:35.956
‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke
